## Quote schema

Every record: `id` (prefix `dvNN-NNNN`, never reused), `source`, `url`, `date`, `speaker`, `stage`, `type`, `themes`, `quote` (verbatim, trims only with ` […] `), `context` (≤25 words), `raw_file` (relative to this folder; Reddit originals are in the shared archive, see below). Optional: `segment`, `source_class`, `engagement`. No usernames. No inference of age, gender or diagnosis.

## Vocabulary

Speakers: `new_mother`, `experienced_mother`, `recovered_parent`, `parent_unspecified`, `partner`, `relative_caregiver`, `advisor`, `professional`, `reviewer`, `skeptic`, `gave_up_parent`. Use `parent_unspecified` unless the author identifies as a mother.

Stages: `newborn_0_8_weeks`, `baby_2_4_months`, `baby_4_6_months`, `baby_6_9_months`, `baby_9_12_months`, `toddler_12_18_months`, `toddler_18_24_months`, `looking_back`, `unknown`.

Types: `trigger_moment`, `pain`, `fear`, `tried_failed`, `desire`, `belief`, `question`, `objection`, `advice_given`, `success_story`, `failure_story`, `regret`, `others_said`, `purchase`, `price_signal`. `purchase` = the author says they bought or paid for something for this problem; `price_signal` = what they say it was worth.

Seed themes (agents may add; document additions in `evidence/reader-notes-*.md`): `what_to_do_all_day`, `awake_time`, `tummy_time`, `tummy_time_hate`, `floor_play`, `rolling`, `sitting`, `crawling`, `pulling_up`, `walking`, `first_words`, `babbling`, `fine_motor`, `milestone_comparison`, `milestone_anxiety`, `corrected_age`, `pediatrician_checkup`, `cdc_milestones`, `wonder_weeks`, `leaps`, `screen_time`, `toys_too_many`, `montessori`, `play_ideas`, `boredom_mum`, `maternal_guilt`, `not_enough_play`, `container_time`, `baby_classes`, `app_tracking`, `information_overload`, `conflicting_advice`, `reassurance_seeking`, `social_comparison`, `grandparent_comments`, `early_intervention_question`, `personalization`, `price_value`.

The other side of the door: Grandparents and in-laws who compare; paediatricians and physios; parents who say 'babies just develop'; Montessori purists; buyers of apps who cancelled.

# Evidence

The round that began 2026-11-18 is in `2026-11/`: post counts by pattern from a random
sample of 20,000 posts. Start at `2026-11/README.md`.
The October 2026 round is in `2026-10/` and is superseded: its counts are of quotes from
a skewed selection, see `../README.md`. Its own README is `2026-10/README.md`.
# Niches

One row per niche. Start here: the row tells you the niche, where its research is,
which knowledge and voice go with her, and which brands sell to her.

| Niche | Status | Research | Knowledge | Voice | Brands |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `baby-development` | active | `~/GitHub/_research/baby-development/` | `knowledge/baby-development/` (not started) | not written yet | mamivio |
| `sleep-baby` | parked | `~/GitHub/_research/sleep-baby/` | none | none | none |
| `sleep-mother` | parked | `~/GitHub/_research/sleep-mother/` | none | none | none |
| `toddler-behaviour` | parked | `~/GitHub/_research/toddler-behaviour/` | none | none | none |
| `pregnancy-birth` | parked | `~/GitHub/_research/pregnancy-birth/` | none | none | none |
| `new-and-expecting-mothers` | research only | `~/GitHub/_research/new-and-expecting-mothers/` | none | none | mamivio (niche selection) |

Status is one of: active, parked (researched, not pursued now), dropped (with the reason
in the avatar file), research only (a market-wide research folder, not a buyer).

The niche name is used unchanged in three places: `library/avatars/<niche>/`,
`~/GitHub/_research/<niche>/`, and this table. It does not change once research is
filed under it. A new understanding of the buyer gets a new niche.

## Definitions

A niche is chosen by the owner from a map of a crowd (`playbooks/new-niche.md`, "The five
steps of research"). Its definition is then one line, the subject and its range, with the counts
behind it. It never says who she is or what her problem is: the deep reading finds the
problem and the avatar says who she is. Before a map exists there is no niche to define,
only a crowd to read. Every deep-reading brief copies the definition word for word, and
`~/GitHub/_research/_tools/check_definition.py` refuses a brief that does not, or a
definition the owner has not confirmed.

### `baby-development`

- **Subject:** The development of a child from birth to 48 months.
- **Confirmed by the owner:** 2026-11-20. The owner set the range ("we are targeting 0 to 48 months"); it was not chosen from a map. Posts about older children are still recorded, as "near", so the counts can show what lies beyond 48 months.

History: until 2026-11-20 the readings stopped at 24 months, a limit carried over from an
older brief without asking the owner.

